       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg. The usual adult dose is 5 mg once daily, and it can be raised to 10 mg. A 50 mg dose could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock, and the effects can last a long time because the half-life is 30 to 50 hours.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the standard starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, sometimes used for frailty or when starting low\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter the order now."
