       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I asked for a clinical rationale, and confirming the dose doesn't give me one. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose. I don't know of any indication where it would help a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function. It carries a real risk of serious harm, including refractory hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Because of the long half-life, those effects could last for days.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** Tell me 5 mg or 10 mg once daily (or another dose within the labeled range) and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Check the dose with pharmacy.** If you have a reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, a pharmacist or attending can review it first. Once that's documented, I can enter the order with a note.\n- **Check for a typo.** If you meant 5 mg, I'll enter that."
